# Printing, line wrapping, and basic C0 controls.

=== Printable characters advance the cursor
size 10x2
input "abc"
screen
  |abc       |
  |          |
cursor 4,1

=== Writing the last column leaves the cursor there with a pending wrap
size 5x2
input "abcde"
screen
  |abcde|
  |     |
cursor 5,1
ref ctlseqs: DECAWM (autowrap is on by default)

=== The next character after a pending wrap goes to the next line
size 5x2
input "abcdef"
screen
  |abcde|
  |f    |
cursor 2,2
ref ctlseqs: DECAWM

=== CR cancels a pending wrap
size 5x2
input "abcde\rX"
screen
  |Xbcde|
  |     |
cursor 2,1

=== Without autowrap, characters overwrite the last column
size 5x2
input "\e[?7labcdefg"
screen
  |abcdg|
  |     |
cursor 5,1
ref ctlseqs: CSI ? 7 l (DECAWM reset)

=== LF moves down without changing the column
size 10x2
input "ab\ncd"
screen
  |ab        |
  |  cd      |
cursor 5,2
ref ctlseqs: LF (line feed mode is reset by default)

=== CR LF starts a new line
size 10x2
input "ab\r\ncd"
screen
  |ab        |
  |cd        |
cursor 3,2

=== BS moves left without erasing
size 10x1
input "abc\b\bX"
screen
  |aXc       |
cursor 3,1

=== BS at the first column does nothing
size 10x1
input "\b\bX"
screen
  |X         |
cursor 2,1

=== HT moves to the next tab stop, every 8 columns by default
size 20x1
input "a\tb\tc"
screen
  |a       b       c   |
cursor 18,1
ref ctlseqs: TAB

=== HT stops at the right margin when there is no further tab stop
size 10x1
input "\t\tX"
screen
  |         X|
cursor 10,1

=== BEL is not displayed
size 10x1
input "a\x07b"
screen
  |ab        |
cursor 3,1

=== A wide character occupies two cells
size 10x1
input "あいa"
screen
  |あいa     |
cursor 6,1
ref Unicode UAX #11: East Asian Wide

=== A wide character that does not fit in the last column wraps to the next line
size 5x2
input "abcdあ"
screen
  |abcd |
  |あ   |
cursor 3,2

=== Insert mode shifts existing characters right
size 10x1
input "abc\r\e[4hX"
screen
  |Xabc      |
cursor 2,1
ref ctlseqs: CSI 4 h (IRM)
